                     /note="MftD, an enzyme found in the mycofactocin
                     biosynthesis locus, performs an oxidative deamination of
                     3-amino-5-[(p-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-4,
                     4-dimethyl-2-pyrrolidinone (AHDP). The resulting compound,
                     now called pre-mycofactocin (PMFT), is a biologically
                     active redox cofactor that can oxidize the
                     non-exchangeable NADH of TIGR03971 family SDR-type
                     oxidoreductases.; MftD, an enzyme found in the
